{"id":"fb3df47c91e4a261","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-orientable.md","title":"Orientable","display":"df-orientable — Orientable","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-orientable","aliases":["58-df-orientable","Orientable"],"display":"df-orientable — Orientable","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-orientation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-orientable"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-orientable</span><span>Orientable</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-orientable — Orientable"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"bc8c800bbf59f617\" href=\"?note=bc8c800bbf59f617\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-orientation.md\">../batch02/58-df-orientation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,n\\in V\">\\(M,n\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Orientable}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Orientable}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (smooth orientability predicate, including the smooth-manifold and nowhere-vanishing top-form data; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bc8c800bbf59f617\" href=\"?note=bc8c800bbf59f617\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-orientation.md\">../batch02/58-df-orientation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S\\)</span> (orientable-manifold predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}orientable} \\vdash \\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S(M,n)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Orientable}_S(M,n)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}orientable} \\vdash \\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S(M,n)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Orientable}_S(M,n)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Orientable: choice of &quot;handedness&quot; at each point that varies continuously</li>\n<li>The compatibility predicate now imports the upstream smooth-manifold and differential-form requirements instead of combining a merely topological manifold with an undeclared <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega^n(M)\">\\(\\Omega^n(M)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Orientation cover: double cover distinguishing orientation; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tilde{M} \\to M\">\\(\\tilde{M} \\to M\\)</span></li>\n<li>Non-orientable examples include <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{RP}^2\">\\(\\mathbb{RP}^2\\)</span>, the Klein bottle, and the Möbius band.</li>\n<li>A connected orientable manifold has two orientations, but the set of orientations is not canonically asserted here to be the group <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Z/2\\mathbb Z\">\\(\\mathbb Z/2\\mathbb Z\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lee, Introduction to Smooth Manifolds</li>\n<li>Hatcher, Algebraic Topology</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-orientation.md","status":"resolved","id":"bc8c800bbf59f617","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-orientation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-orientation.md","status":"resolved","id":"bc8c800bbf59f617","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Orientable}_S\\subseteq V^2$ (smooth orientability predicate, including the smooth-manifold and nowhere-vanishing top-form data; see [[../batch02/58-df-orientation.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,n\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Orientable}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}orientable} \\vdash \\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S(M,n)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Orientable}_S(M,n)","display":true},{"tex":"\\Omega^n(M)","display":false},{"tex":"\\tilde{M} \\to M","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{RP}^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb Z/2\\mathbb Z","display":false}],"bytes":1403,"backlinks":[{"id":"34946ea21ee88f10","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{OrientableManifold}_S$ (orientable-manifold predicate, see [[58-df-orientable.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-924","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-orientable.md|58-df-orientable]]（batch01）"}],"outgoing":["bc8c800bbf59f617"]}